From pravinj at gmail.com  Sun Dec  5 19:23:03 2004
From: pravinj at gmail.com (Pravin Jadhav)
Date: Sun, 05 Dec 2004 14:23:03 -0500
Subject: Re: parameter constraints in nlme?
In-Reply-To: <41B09040.24563.1860314@localhost>
References: <41B09040.24563.1860314@localhost>
Message-ID: <679f8b3f04120511235fdac882@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Ronald,

For a different problem, we were looking for a similar feature in
NLME. As it turns out, there is no straightforward solution. I doubt
if one can constrain parameters in NLME implemented in S-Plus. But one
could fix some of the fixed effects. But it is tricky if you are
interested in estimating corresponding random effects. Let me know if
you are interested in that strategy and need help.

Other option is to use software like NONMEM
(http://www.globomaxservice.com/products/nonmem.html) that is very
flexible in terms of model specification and probably convenient to
use.

Hope it helps.

Pravin 

