Subject: minimization with restriction in S+
Message-ID: <6.2.0.14.0.20041208095150.01cc1108@wubios.wustl.edu>

Dear List:

Does anyone know how to minimize a function with restriction, i.e., to 
minimize a function f(w) with 3 parameters w={w1,w2,w3} and with w1^2 + 
w2^2 + w3^2=1? In addition, only f(w) can be evaluated, and f'(w) and 
f''(w) can not be derived.

At beginning I tried a naive way to minimize with nlminb(start = c(0.1, 
0.1), objective = ob, lower = -1, upper = 1), where f(w) is minimized only 
based on w1 and w2 while I set w3=(+ -)sqrt(1-w1^2 -w2^2). this approach 
does not work because sometimes w3=NA.

is there any function available for such a problem?

Many thanks in advance for your suggestions!

Feng Gao

