From andy_liaw at merck.com  Wed Dec  8 16:40:26 2004
From: andy_liaw at merck.com (Liaw, Andy)
Date: Wed, 08 Dec 2004 11:40:26 -0500
Subject: Re: minimization with restriction in S+
Message-ID: <3A822319EB35174CA3714066D590DCD50994E3F7@usrymx25.merck.com>

One possibility is to re-parameterize the problem.  A simpler example: let's
say you want to minimize f(x1, x2) with the constraint is x1^2 + x2^2 = 1.
The constraint is on the unit circle, and the problem can be effectively
reduced to only one parameter.  Let x1=sin(theta) and x2=cos(theta) with
theta in [0, 2*pi], you can re-define f in terms of theta, minimize that,
then back-transform to get (x1, x2).  You get the idea.

HTH,
Andy

