Dear Ronald,

This problem is well suited for the software package AD Model Builder,
and in particular its random effects module:

http://otter-rsch.com/admbre/admbre.html

AD Model Builder is very flexible, and it is possible to implement the models
you describe. Because ADMB takes a very different approach to random 
effects models it is also easy to put constraints on parameters. There
are of course limits to the size of the model (the range of i,j,k), but
for the number of levels of i,j,k you describe there should be no problem.

A comparison of AD Model Builder and NLME can be found here:

http://otter-rsch.com/admbre/examples/pheno/pheno.html

hans
