Message-ID: <6.1.0.6.2.20041217091159.06170498@mailhost.blackmesacapital.com>

Actually, read.table() does know the total size of the data set before 
invoking scan() -- because it invokes count.fields() on the file 
first.  (I.e., it reads the file twice.)  The number of records is stored 
in the variable nrec.  So, it's an easy change to make read.table() to 
preallocate space for scan() (using the 'what=' argument).  Maybe there's 
some good reason for not preallocating, but I suspect that it's more likely 
just a case of over-mature code.

-- Tony Plate

