Under Windows there is also win3().
Under Unix, there is unix().

What shell dos() uses is set by the ComSpec variable, AFAICS.  Under 
NT-based versions of Windows it defaults to cmd.exe, and that understands 
"2>&1".  Under 16-bit versions of dos() (Win 95/98/ME) it defaults to 
command.com, which does not, but some alternative shells do.

